{
  "id": "ACT.25",
  "number": "25",
  "bookId": "ACT",
  "reference": "Acts 25",
  "verseCount": 27,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "25",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "ACT 25"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "25",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now when Festus had come into his province, after three days he went up to Jerusalem from Caesarea. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the chief priests and the principal men of the Jews informed him against Paul; and they urged him, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "asking as a favor to have the man sent to Jerusalem, planning an ambush to kill him on the way. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Festus replied that Paul was being kept at Caesarea, and that he himself intended to go there shortly. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“So,” said he, “let the men of authority among you go down with me, and if there is anything wrong about the man, let them accuse him.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.5"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When he had stayed among them not more than eight or ten days, he went down to Caesarea; and the next day he took his seat on the tribunal and ordered Paul to be brought. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And when he had come, the Jews who had gone down from Jerusalem stood about him, bringing against him many serious charges which they could not prove. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Paul said in his defense, “Neither against the law of the Jews, nor against the temple, nor against Caesar have I offended at all.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Festus, wishing to do the Jews a favor, said to Paul, “Do you wish to go up to Jerusalem, and there be tried on these charges before me?” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Paul said, “I am standing before Caesar's tribunal, where I ought to be tried; to the Jews I have done no wrong, as you know very well. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If then I am a wrongdoer, and have committed anything for which I deserve to die, I do not seek to escape death; but if there is nothing in their charges against me, no one can give me up to them. I appeal to Caesar.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Festus, when he had conferred with his council, answered, “You have appealed to Caesar; to Caesar you shall go.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.12"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now when some days had passed, Agrippa the king and Bernice arrived at Caesarea to welcome Festus. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And as they stayed there many days, Festus laid Paul's case before the king, saying, “There is a man left prisoner by Felix; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and when I was at Jerusalem, the chief priests and the elders of the Jews gave information about him, asking for sentence against him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I answered them that it was not the custom of the Romans to give up any one before the accused met the accusers face to face, and had opportunity to make his defense concerning the charge laid against him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When therefore they came together here, I made no delay, but on the next day took my seat on the tribunal and ordered the man to be brought in. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When the accusers stood up, they brought no charge in his case of such evils as I supposed; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "but they had certain points of dispute with him about their own superstition and about one Jesus, who was dead, but whom Paul asserted to be alive. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Being at a loss how to investigate these questions, I asked whether he wished to go to Jerusalem and be tried there regarding them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But when Paul had appealed to be kept in custody for the decision of the emperor, I commanded him to be held until I could send him to Caesar.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Agrippa said to Festus, “I should like to hear the man myself.” “Tomorrow,” said he, “you shall hear him.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.22"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So on the morrow Agrippa and Bernice came with great pomp, and they entered the audience hall with the military tribunes and the prominent men of the city. Then by command of Festus Paul was brought in. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Festus said, “King Agrippa and all who are present with us, you see this man about whom the whole Jewish people petitioned me, both at Jerusalem and here, shouting that he ought not to live any longer. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But I found that he had done nothing deserving death; and as he himself appealed to the emperor, I decided to send him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But I have nothing definite to write to my lord about him. Therefore I have brought him before you, and, especially before you, King Agrippa, that, after we have examined him, I may have something to write. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ACT 25:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For it seems to me unreasonable, in sending a prisoner, not to indicate the charges against him.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ACT.25.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ACT.25.27"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "next": {
    "id": "ACT.26",
    "number": "26",
